#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
# NexusBackup OS update agent (plan.md 12.1, docs/release.md "Updates").
#
#   nexus-update tick       what nexus-update.service runs (timer every 15 min + path unit):
#                           handle a pending request, stage when the last check is older
#                           than the check interval, apply inside the maintenance window
#   nexus-update stage      fetch + verify the signed image, stage it download-only
#                           (an unplanned reboot does NOT apply it)
#   nexus-update apply      reboot into the staged image now
#   nexus-update rollback   make the previous deployment the default and reboot
#   nexus-update status     print the status JSON (also written to the control dir)
#   nexus-update status --json
#                           print the web UI view (docs/phase12-contract.md §5; also the
#                           "api" member of status.json, which nexus-web-api reads)
#
# Control directory (default /var/lib/nexus/update, 2770 root:nexus-catalog, see
# tmpfiles.d/nexus-update.conf) is the interface for web-api and scheduler:
#   request      written by the control plane: one word, "stage" | "apply" | "rollback"
#                ("apply" = install now: stage first if nothing is staged, then reboot into it);
#                consumed (deleted) by the next tick, which nexus-update.path starts at once
#   window       optional override of NEXUS_UPDATE_WINDOW, e.g. "Sun 03:00 120" or "off"
#   inhibit      present and younger than 6 h: automatic (window) apply is postponed;
#                the scheduler touches it while jobs run. Admin "apply" ignores it.
#   status.json  written here (0640): booted/staged/rollback image, last check, last result,
#                and "api" (the view GET /api/v1/updates returns)
#
# Signature enforcement: bootc only consults /etc/containers/policy.json when the
# deployment's origin is "ostree-image-signed" (bootc status: signature "containerPolicy").
# An origin with signature "insecure" (the default after a plain install or switch) is
# fetched with skopeo --insecure-policy. stage therefore refuses `bootc upgrade` on such
# a host and runs `bootc switch --enforce-container-sigpolicy <repo>:<tag>` instead, which
# fixes the origin for every later upgrade.
#
# Pre-update checks (Phase 14b): before it stages or applies an image, nexus-update runs
# `nexus-diag checks` and refuses while a check with severity >= 3 fails (disk full,
# clock not synchronised, catalog or audit chain broken, SELinux not enforcing, ...).
# The refusal is the last result ("refused: ..."), the api view shows status "blocked"
# with the failing checks. Rollback is never blocked. If nexus-diag itself cannot run,
# the update goes ahead (a broken checker must not block the update that fixes it).
# NEXUS_UPDATE_DIAG=off (environment or update.conf) skips the checks.

